skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: move proveo from sbx v2 kits (built-in agent + kind: mixin, -t image) to v3 workloads, v3 as source of truth
' would touch: internal/sbx/kit.go, internal/sbx/agents.go, internal/sbx/sbx.go, internal/sbx/version.go
' would touch: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Spec, startupCommands, agentCredentials), internal/sbx/run.go (RunArgs)
' would touch: internal/imagebuild/**, defs/*/Dockerfile, cmd/proveo/testdata/plan/*.golden
' would touch: internal/backend/sandbox/own_agent_test.go, internal/sbx/sbx_test.go
' supersedes on landing: _spec/internal/sbx/sbx-kit-contract.puml (v2 field contract), the v2 half of _spec/_experiments/sbx-kit-capabilities.puml
' status: PLANNED 2026-10-22 — user: "Plan a v3 migration", "use v3 guidelines as source of truth, downstream from there (port mapping)".
' _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
'
' ── SOURCES (read 2026-10-22) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
'   github.com/docker/sandbox-kit-spec @ f53ac62: docs/spec/SPEC-v3.md,
'     capabilities/com.docker.sandbox/{sbx,lifecycle,credential,port}@1,
'     skills/migrate-kit-to-v3/FIELD-MAPPING.md ("where this document and the
'     code disagree, the code wins")
'   github.com/docker/sbx-kits-contrib/tree/v3/claude (= docker.io/docker/sbx-kit-claude)
'   docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/{,use-kits/,kits-v2/,author/**}
'   docker/sbx-releases notes v0.45.0–v0.49.2; issues #696 #710 #738 #614 #474
'
' ── WHY (MEASURED) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   * "Docker recommends v3 kits"; "V2 remains supported and is not deprecated".
'   * Built-in names (claude, codex, cursor, opencode) select v2, so proveo's
'     v2 split (built-in agent + mixin + -t image) can never take a v3 mixin.
'   * The recipe departure behind the flavor warning (shell-docker image run
'     as `claude`, sbx-kit-capabilities.puml:473) exists only on the -t path.
'     [Inference, untested] a v3 workload takes no -t, so no warning.
'
' ── v2 → v3, FIELD BY FIELD (from FIELD-MAPPING + proveo's Spec) ─────────────
'   v2 (today)                         v3 (target)
'   sbx run <builtin> -t IMG --kit D   sbx run ./proveo-<target> (own workload)
'   kind: mixin <target>-posture       kind: workload, dir proveo-<target>
'   kind: sandbox (cecli own-agent)    kind: workload (same shape as the rest)
'   sandbox.image: IMG                 <stem>.dockerfile: FROM IMG
'   environment.variables              ENV in the recipe (per-run values: see Q2)
'   setup.startup (root seed)          lifecycle@1 install hook, user "0"
'   setup.startup (agent seed)         lifecycle@1 startup hook, user agent
'   permissions.network.allow          network-policy@1 (runtime allow; singleton)
'   credentials[].apiKey (own-agent)   credential@1 service, phase: runtime
'   built-in agent's credential        COPIED into proveo's descriptor: a FROM
'                                      does not carry a published kit's
'                                      capabilities (author/base-images/)
'   image ENTRYPOINT as PID 1          sbx@1: the host launches the agent
'   descriptor file spec.yaml          <stem>.yaml — NEVER spec.yaml (#738)
'
' ── PORTS (DOWNSTREAM OF v3) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' port@1: "A Kit cannot pin a host port … users pin host ports through the
' runtime's own UX, not the descriptor"; the runtime allocates an ephemeral
' loopback port for a kit-declared one. `-p [[IP:]HOST:]GUEST` and `sbx ports`
' ARE that runtime UX and are not v2-only. So the 1–9 prefix rule
' (_spec/internal/devports/dev-ports.puml, commit b424d23) stays on `-p`, and
' proveo declares NO port@1 for dev ports: it would add a second, ephemeral
' binding for the same guest port. [Inference] Revisit if probe P3 shows sbx
' merges a kit port with a -p for the same guest port.
'
' ── CONSTRAINTS THAT SHAPE THE DESIGN ──────────────────────────────────────
'   C1 v3 needs sbx ≥ 0.45 (lifecycle, credential, network-policy, port, sbx@1);
'      SBX_AGENT and kit.env arrive in 0.48. Verified {0.42–0.44} drop out.
'   C2 CORRECTED by P1: `-t` with a positional LOCAL v3 workload is accepted
'      and replaces the kit-built image (the binary's refusal string covers
'      some other case, not this one).
'   C3 sbx pulls a kit's base image; "It can't use images stored only in your
'      host's Docker image store"; local kits build in sandbox `sbx-kit-builder`.
'   C4 a local kit's build context is its own directory (#710): no COPY from
'      the proveo checkout unless the files are staged into the kit dir.
'   C5 agent name = kit dir / repo last component; must not be a built-in.
'   C6 one owner per (service, phase) credential; no duplicate `provides`.
'   C7 hook env is deny-by-default ("a hook sees only what it declares").
'
' ── OPEN QUESTIONS (each needs a measured answer before code) ──────────────
'   Q1 IMAGE SOURCE (C3): host-built proveo images vs sbx-kit-builder.
'      P2 decides between (a) push proveo images to a registry sbx can pull
'      (local registry for :local), (b) the kit dockerfile IS the image
'      recipe (imagebuild emits kits), (c) a supported local-image path.
'   Q2 PER-RUN VALUES: today's mixin carries host-resolved env (paths, sid,
'      clone links). v3 env lives in the image; candidates: kit args
'      (`--kit-arg`, honored for local kits since 0.49.1), kit.env (0.48),
'      or a run-time file read by the startup hook.
'   Q3 CREDENTIALS: copy sbx-kit-claude's credential@1 (apiKey x-api-key +
'      OAuth sentinel, ~/.claude/.credentials.json) and its install hooks,
'      or compose a kit set FROM docker/sbx-kit-claude + a proveo mixin
'      (keeps Docker's credential code; Claude Code pin moves to Docker's
'      kit; mixin image layers count toward the 44-layer limit).
'
' ── PROBES (P0, each ≤ 2 min, throwaway names, cleaned up) ──────────────────
'   P1 `sbx create -t IMG ./v3kit` and `-t` with a v2 local kit: what C2 covers
'   P2 v3 workload with FROM <host-only image>: does sbx-kit-builder resolve it?
'   P3 kit port@1 + `-p H:P` for the same P: coexist, merge, or refuse?
'   P4 v3 workload FROM proveo/claudecode:local run as proveo-claudecode: no
'      flavor warning, Claude Code launches, OAuth credential flows
'   P5 install vs startup hook timing against proveo-seed and proveo-await-seed
'      (_spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml)
'
' ── PROBE RESULTS (MEASURED 2026-10-22, sbx 0.49.2, macOS arm64) ───────────
'   P0 minimal local workload (FROM shell-docker-0.5.0, sbx@1 only): built
'      as `sbx-kit-src:<dir>-<hash>` in sbx's store, created in 18s,
'      SBX_AGENT=<dir name>, user agent. The build pulls the frontend
'      docker.io/docker/sandbox-kit:3, so building needs Docker Hub.
'   P1 the same kit + `-t docker/sandbox-templates:shell-docker-0.5.0`:
'      accepted (10s); Image = the -t image, SBX_AGENT still the kit's, and
'      the flavor warning returns ("built for the shell agent but you are
'      using probe-v3shell"). So the warning belongs to -t, not to v2.
'   P2 workload FROM proveo/claudecode:local (host Docker + sbx store): built
'      and booted; Claude Code 2.1.308 runs as user claude; NO flavor warning.
'   P2b workload FROM proveo-probe/layers44:local (host Docker store only):
'      the build RESOLVED it (image ready), so C3 does not hold for local
'      kits: sbx-kit-builder reads the host Docker store. The boot then hung:
'      the kit build adds ≥1 layer, and 44 + ≥1 hits the 45-layer limit
'      (_spec/_devops/sandbox-template-rebase.puml, FLAT BASE). Layer budget
'      for a FROM image under a v3 kit is therefore ≤ 43.
'   BUILD PATH: with a host Docker engine present, a local kit builds on IT,
'      not in sbx-kit-builder: `docker buildx build ./<kit> -t sbx-kit-src:…`
'      against the current context (here OrbStack, …/.orbstack/run/docker.sock).
'      That is why P2/P2b resolve host-only images, and it couples proveo's
'      v3 launch to the host engine's health (a hung engine hangs `sbx create`
'      at "building…", measured after P5).
'   Q1 → (c) holds for local runs: FROM the host-built proveo image, no
'      registry. Published images still need a registry (pull path, C3).
'   P3 port@1 alone: sbx publishes localhost:<ephemeral> → 8099. port@1 +
'      `-p 18099:8099`: ONE binding, 127.0.0.1:18099 → 8099 — the operator's
'      -p replaces the kit's ephemeral host port. So declaring port@1 AND
'      pinning with -p is safe; the PORTS section's "no port@1" is revised:
'      port@1 may name the port (permission surface), -p keeps the 1–9 rule.
'   P4 workload proveo-claudecode FROM proveo/claudecode:local with the
'      published kit's credential@1 (service anthropic, apiKey + OAuth
'      sentinels), network-policy@1 and its root trust-seed install hook:
'      created in 16s, no flavor warning, SBX_AGENT=proveo-claudecode, user
'      claude, ~/.claude/.credentials.json holds the sentinel, and
'      `claude -p` answered through sbx's OAuth proxy (daemon: POST
'      /sandbox/<n>/credentials 200). Q3 → copying the credential block works.
'   P5 hooks with 4s sleeps, timestamps in the guest (create t0):
'        install (root)    +10.7 → +14.7
'        startup (agent)   +15.5 → +19.5   (sequential, after install)
'        create returned   ≈ +20           (it waits for both)
'        `sbx run --name` on the created sandbox: agent at +21.3; startup did
'        NOT rerun on attach.
'      So create-then-run gates the agent on BOTH hook phases — the v2
'      "startup never gates the agent" trap (proveo-await-seed) does not
'      apply to that flow. [Inference] a one-shot `sbx run <kit>` still
'      starts the agent alongside startup hooks (docs); untested.
'   Q2 probe: `sbx create -e PROVEO_PROBE_VAR=per-run-42 ./<v3 workload>`:
'      the agent env sees it, and an install hook that declares
'      `env: [PROVEO_PROBE_VAR]` sees it too. So per-run values keep riding
'      on `-e` (today's mechanism); hooks list the names they read (C7).
'   P6 ~/.claude.json persistence, real proveo_sync_config restore/save
'      against a scratch host copy (mcpServers, claudeInChromeDefaultEnabled,
'      userID, project /old; mtime older than create):
'        a) upstream root hook verbatim (`> ~/.claude.json`), then restore:
'           restore SKIPS (host older, the `-nt` rule), the file keeps only
'           upstream's 3 keys, and save OVERWRITES the host copy with them.
'        b) restore, then proveo's accept_workspace_trust merge: every host
'           key survives in the sandbox and on the host, plus workspace trust.
'      Also measured: an install hook that exits non-zero ABORTS `sbx create`
'      ("failed to apply kit to sandbox"); hooks run as `docker run --rm -u
'      <user> <kit image> sh -c 'env -i <allowlist> sh -c …'` — dash, so
'      bash-only code needs `bash -c`, and every proveo hook must never fail
'      the create (as the v2 seedNeverAbort wrapper already ensures).
'   P7 launch: workload ENTRYPOINT ["sh","-c","<log $0 $*>","launcher"]
'      CMD ["default-cmd"]:
'        PID 1 is sbx's keepalive (`sh -c trap …; sleep infinity & wait`),
'        never the image ENTRYPOINT → proveo_sbx_passthrough is dead code
'        under sbx@1 (DELETE).
'        `sbx run --name X` (no args) launched `launcher default-cmd`, i.e.
'        ENTRYPOINT + CMD.
'        `sbx run --name X -- extra1 extra2` launched `sh extra1 extra2`
'        ("cannot open extra1"): trailing args replace EVERYTHING after
'        ENTRYPOINT[0]. So when proveo adds launch flags it sends
'        launch[1:] + flags (e.g. --dangerously-skip-permissions …) — the
'        v2 OwnAgentCommand rule, now for every harness.
'      CORRECTED 2026-10-26 (MEASURED, sbx 0.49.2, ENTRYPOINT
'      ["/bin/echo","EP0","EP1"] CMD ["C1"]): the rule splits on the
'      trailing command's first word.
'        `-- A B`       → `A B`               (argv0 + trailing: replace)
'        `-- /x A`      → `/x A`              (replace)
'        `-- -x A`      → `EP0 EP1 C1 -x A`   (leading flag: APPEND to
'        `-- --flag A`  → `EP0 EP1 C1 --flag A`  ENTRYPOINT + CMD)
'        `-- -- A B`    → `EP0 EP1 C1 -- A B` (a bare -- appends too)
'      Every proveo image's ENTRYPOINT is `dumb-init -- /entrypoint.sh`, so
'      launch[1:] opened with `--`: sbx appended it, /entrypoint.sh got
'      `-- /entrypoint.sh -s …`, and hermes exited 2 ("'/entrypoint.sh' is
'      not a hermes command") on every scheduled muse run since 2026-10-22.
'      Kit-launched harnesses only duplicated their own flag
'      (`claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --dangerously-skip-…`).
'      LaunchArgs now sends flags alone when they lead (append), else
'      launch[1:] without dumb-init's `--` (replace); sbx.Launched models
'      both. Tests: TestLaunchArgsFollowSbxsAppendAndReplaceRule,
'      TestLaunchedIsWhatSbxRunStarts.
'      Probe hazards seen on the way: `sbx run` under `script` (pty) stalls
'      at "building…" on an unanswered terminal query (OSC 11), and killing
'      it orphaned a `docker buildx` while OrbStack's API hung; `orb restart
'      docker` recovered it (6s).
'
' ── LIVE RUNS (2026-10-23/24, operator, CLI dev@3ac97ff-v3 from this branch) ─
'   hermes (no published kit, image ENTRYPOINT): created, launched; banner
'      showed 64 skills incl. the muse ones (linked-dirs) on muse-glimmer.
'   claudecode: first blocked retiring v2-era sandboxes (f8781ef6 never
'      answered the clone probe — old layered image; hermes-0ad8f1e5 broken
'      by an earlier shim kill), then the kit build failed: "open
'      claude-context.md: no such file or directory" — agent-context@1's
'      contentFile is kit-relative and was not vendored. Fixed: the kit's
'      files travel with UpstreamKit.Files and are written beside the
'      descriptor; a test fails for any unvendored contentFile.
'      Re-run on cb7b344 (2026-10-24): PASSED — the operator reported it
'      worked; sbx lists proveo-claudecode-f8781ef6 with agent
'      proveo-claudecode (the v3 workload, not the built-in "claude").
'   RETIRE FIX (user: "Offer remove-anyway"): a sandbox that never answers the
'      clone probe can be removed on a headed yes that lists its
'      refs/sandboxes/<name>/ mirrors; kit-lifecycle.puml records it.
'
' ── DECISIONS (2026-10-22, user, on the evidence above) ─────────────────────
'   Q1 "Kit FROM proveo image": <stem>.dockerfile = FROM proveo/<target>:<tag>;
'      :local resolves from the host engine, published tags pull. Images stay
'      ≤ 43 layers (the kit adds ≥ 1).
'   Q2 "Keep -e": per-run values stay on `-e`; each hook lists the names it
'      reads in `env:` (C7).
'   Q3 "if docker sbx supports any functionality proveo has, prefer using
'      upstream (#2 in this case)": copy the published kit's credential@1,
'      network-policy AND lifecycle hooks (and volumes, agent-context) into
'      proveo's workload, and DELETE the proveo code they make redundant.
'      Keep proveo-only behaviour only where upstream lacks it or a recorded
'      decision contradicts it (overlap table: pending research).
'   Q3 EXCEPTIONS (user, after the overlap research and P6):
'      * MCP gateway: "mcp can be a new row under the sbx's egress in
'        internal/choiceui. If we only have on/off so be it" — copy the
'        upstream gateway hooks, render them only when that row is on.
'      * ~/.claude.json: "#1 but explain this issue further; we don't want to
'        vibe the wheel" → P6 measured the loss; DO NOT copy upstream's root
'        `> ~/.claude.json` hook. proveo's restore runs first and
'        accept_workspace_trust (an existing merge) also sets
'        bypassPermissionsModeAccepted and hasCompletedOnboarding and trusts
'        `/`. The one deliberate skip of an upstream hook.
'      * upstream claude-context.md assumes CLAUDE_ENV_FILE: "Set
'        CLAUDE_ENV_FILE in the base" → ENV CLAUDE_ENV_FILE=/etc/sandbox-
'        persistent.sh in defs/base (BASH_ENV already points there); copy
'        agent-context@1 as is.
'   ROLLOUT "hard switch to v3, compatibility upgrade. Drop support for sbx
'      versions that aren't v3": no v2 fallback, no flag. MinVersion → 0.45
'      (v3); Verified keeps only series measured on the v3 path (0.49 today;
'      0.45–0.48 warn until measured); init's Release → 0.49.2.
'   CURSOR "Keep upstream, lose the deny list": copy the kit's
'      `files: cli-config.json (overwrite:false)` verbatim; proveo's cursor
'      deny-list default goes.
'   CODEX "Delete dup keys, merge the rest": approval/sandbox leave
'      defs/codex/defaults/config.toml (upstream's install hook owns them);
'      proveo merges its remaining keys into the file upstream wrote.
'   LAUNCH "create, then run": `sbx create` (hooks finish, P5) then
'      `sbx run --name`; proveo-await-seed is a safety net, not the gate.
'
' ── STEP 8 DELETIONS (2026-10-24, "prefer using upstream, delete proveo code") ─
'   DONE: proveo_sbx_passthrough + _proveo_in_sbx + the six entrypoint calls
'     (v3 PID 1 is sbx's keepalive, P7; the keepalive test went, the
'     await-seed identity test stayed); WithMCPGatewayPolicy; KitEnvVars;
'     OwnAgentCommand; AgentFor, ShellAgent, EnvAgentKit/AgentKitEnabled/
'     DeclaresOwnAgent + PROVEO_SBX_AGENT_KIT; the v2 Kit/KitCredential*/
'     KitEnv/KitSetup/KitSandbox*/KitPermissions/KitNet types, WriteKit,
'     KitSchemaVersion(V2); template.go whole (EnsureTemplate, ReloadTemplate,
'     HasTemplate, receipts) + PROVEO_SBX_RELOAD + the CLI template hooks —
'     the recipe's FROM resolves from the host engine (P2), so launchSandbox
'     preflights the image on every run instead of asking sbx's store.
'   KEPT: KitCommand (the hook intermediate SeedCommand returns), BuiltinAgent
'     (agent identity: claudecode → claude for auth and the local-model tools).
'   MEASURED: `sbx kit validate --offline <workload dir>` refuses a v3 source
'     kit ("no kit builder configured"); validation needs the daemon's builder.
'   E2E (user: "Full v3 port"): ladder rungs are v3 (capability-ladder.puml);
'     sbx_test checks the workload dir, the v3 descriptor shape and `sbx kit
'     validate` (skips when sbx needs a kit builder); startup_dispatch pins P5;
'     chrome/adb/resume probes create from a minimal workload
'     (e2e/workload_v3_test.go); print-mode parsers read the `# sandbox` create
'     line (env, mounts) and the `# agent` run line (trailing args). The
'     offline and print-mode e2e tests PASS locally (MEASURED); sandbox-creating
'     ones await a live climb.
'
' ── ORDER OF WORK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   1 probes P1–P5 → record results here (MEASURED)
'   2 user decisions on Q1–Q3
'   3 internal/sbx: v3 Kit types + writer (<stem>.yaml + <stem>.dockerfile,
'     `# syntax=docker/sandbox-kit:3`), unknown-field-free (SPEC §1.2)
'   4 Spec(): one workload per run; startupCommands → lifecycle hooks;
'     agentCredentials → credential@1; allow → network-policy@1
'   5 RunArgs: positional kit, no -t, keep -p (ports section)
'   6 MinVersion 0.45, Verified series update, init Release ≥ 0.45
'   7 goldens + own_agent_test + contract test against the spec's examples
'   8 retire the v2 renderer; supersede sbx-kit-contract.puml
title sbx kit v3 migration — v3 is the source of truth, ports downstream

rectangle "today (v2)" as V2 {
  component "sbx built-in agent\nclaude · codex · cursor · opencode" as BUILTIN <<cloud>>
  component "-t proveo/<target>:local\n(shell-docker base)" as TIMG <<app>>
  component "kind: mixin <target>-posture\nenv · startup · allow" as MIX <<app>>
}
rectangle "target (v3)" as V3 {
  component "workload ./proveo-<target>\n<stem>.yaml + <stem>.dockerfile" as WL <<app>>
  component "FROM proveo image\n(source: Q1)" as FROMIMG <<app>>
  component "sbx@1 · lifecycle@1 · credential@1\nnetwork-policy@1" as CAPS <<app>>
}
component "-p <k>P:P\n(runtime UX, unchanged)" as PORTS <<host>>
database "probes P1–P5\nthen Q1–Q3" as GATE <<db>>

BUILTIN -[hidden]-> TIMG
TIMG -[hidden]-> MIX
V2 --> GATE : migrate after
GATE --> V3
WL --> FROMIMG
WL --> CAPS
V2 --> PORTS
V3 --> PORTS
@enduml
